{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1547607-2-5e-help-dig-ourselves-out-of-a-hole","id":1547607,"title":"2.5E - Help dig ourselves out of a hole.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-01-06T15:17:33-08:00","id":1547607,"title":"2.5E - Help dig ourselves out of a hole.","content":"So the campaign I am in is doing Return of the Scarlett Empress. And I think we've sunk ourselves. So any suggestions on what we can do to dig ourselves out is appreciated.<br /> <br /> The Unconquered Sun is Dead, the Ebon Dragon is in creation and killed the elemental dragon of Earth. Whitewall is destroyed. We have stolen the reality engines from Gethamene and they're at the Invisible Fortress.<br /> <br /> The infernals have the Opal Spire. We infiltrated the Opal Spire and took the Protoshinmaic vortex that powers reality engines. We've been fleeing via the one Celestial circle cloud spell and the tornado spell, which the Twilight and Zeniff have been using to let rest. Only problem is that the Infernals have a whole of first age air ships. So they're following us.<br /> <br /> Anywho, long story short we figure we need to deal with someone. We're up in the north, and so figure the closest place to do seek a deal and find help would be the one Deathlord at the Fortress of Crimson Ice. Only, not knowing a whole lot about the Lover Clad in the Raiment of Tears, we ask for an audience.<br /> <br /> My character, the eclipse, has the Overindulgence Temperance flaw, so he hit limit break and is in a pile of creatures doing unspeakable things.<br /> The twilight is passed out from not having enough willpower to resist drugs and liquor being offered.<br /> <br /> Which leaves only the Night Caste and the Zeniff (we have no Dawn).<br /> <br /> Part of the problem is that the DM says the Fortress of Crimson Ice is set up much the same way as Traveler's Road. Which means attacking someone makes you want to commit suicide. And so taking someone against their will has consequences.<br /> And while we have magic items/deathlord bodies to trade, it is obvious that The Lover doesn't think she needs to trade anything since she can seduce us. The Night and Zeniff could flee, but the Infernals are right outside her lands waiting.<br /> <br /> So.. we're kind of screwed.<br /> <br /> We could use suggestions on how to dig ourselves out of this hole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-06T22:47:04-08:00","id":1547613,"title":"","content":"Play into that belief to leverage towards your own goals? I don't remember what she wanted in second edition aside from a lament configuration, for the off chance of something new, but see if you can think of a way to essentially have her figure you lot are able to be seduced into service along the lines of a goal she wants. Something like trying to use you lot to take out TED because the dragon is unlikely to leave the Lover's territory to her. Failing that maybe leverage your continued presence and existence as a problem, like convince her that you lot staying there is a danger if you're not noticeably leaving the territory in a way that makes it more important to hunt your circle than picking a fight with her and hers directly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-08T06:44:27-08:00","id":1547633,"title":"","content":"I'd ask what your Storyteller wants from you at this point.<br /> <br /> The compulsion to kill yourself was considered too powerful for normal social combat hence why Abyssals don\u2019t have it, as thematic as it would've been Neph recognised it could genuinely ruin someone's fun and destroy a game group. The Traveler's Road effect was basically intended to be a one time thing to evoke a certain mood while travelling through a really dangerous area rather than PCs being at a genuine risk of breaking the rules and being forced to commit suicide.<br /> <br /> Putting it in a hostile environment like a Deathlord\u2019s fortress is a choice that your storyteller made.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T21:30:01-08:00","id":1547709,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a>, it sounds like your Storyteller may have worked you into a dead end not *entirely* of your own making - and they probably need to make the next move.<br /> <br /> What exactly are you hoping to get from The Lover, besides apparently a fire in which to hide from the frying pan you jumped out of? What's her motivation now, given everything that has happened in the lands of the living? Does she benefit from helping you? Heck, does she benefit from entraping you, if it keeps an Infernal army on her doorstep?<br /> <br /> What's going on outside the Fortress that might change the circumstances enough for you to find a path out? What do the Infernals want, if anything, besides your death? Are they just chilling out hoping the Lover will kill you instead? Do they want the PSV enough to come in after it?<br /> <br /> Do you have any allies who might show up to help you escape? Maybe a Sidereal survivor or Black Nadir-type Lunar who can get in through the Labyrinth and lead you out the same way?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}